Interactive USD edits of point instancers with deduplicated mesh prototypes (HDARNOLD_GEOM_DEDUP=2)

Two point instancers have identical quad prototypes, and a quad mesh identical to them is not instanced: the render
delegate deduplicates all three in mode 2 (all identical meshes share their arnold geometry). The single mesh leaves
the dedup group and joins it again, the displayColor and points of one prototype are edited, becoming different from
the others and identical again, and the other point instancer and the single mesh are removed. The stage is
re-rendered after each edit. Covers the fix of the dedup incremental updates (#2797).
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
